	<p>I’m a Salesforce CRM Engineer and M.Sc. Computer Science student at the <b>University of Paderborn</b>, based in Paderborn, Germany. I have two years of hands-on Salesforce experience, including administration, automation, data quality, user support, and deployment workflows.</p>

	<p>At Tata Consultancy Services, I configured Salesforce experiences, created reporting and dashboards, and helped make business processes more reliable with Flow, validation rules, and Apex. I particularly enjoy translating a messy real-world process into a system people can confidently use.</p>

	<p>Alongside my studies, I’m deepening my software engineering foundations through web security and data science coursework. I’m also actively studying AI concepts independently, and plan to take Machine Learning and Agentic Software Engineering courses at the University of Paderborn. I approach AI as an engineering discipline that benefits from clear problem definition, responsible use, and careful evaluation.</p>

	<p>I’m beginning to share that learning through this site’s blog, covering AI, software engineering, developer tools, and lessons from projects. I’m seeking a Werkstudent role where I can contribute to CRM, cloud, software engineering, or AI-focused work while continuing to learn in a collaborative team.</p>

	<p>Outside technology, I enjoy squash and swimming, and I’m a member of the International Students’ Representation at the University of Paderborn.</p>

